    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "I think that is already going on with a lot of stuff that you'll get through research colleges, universities, government in just the last ten years. I look at my own farm. The number of riparian buffers, grass, waterways, cover crops, really surgical application of nutrients. When you're getting the grids down to not a quarter acre, you know, but even a fraction of that in terms of how you apply nutrients. That's all playing into number one, what makes us way lower emitter of CO2 through agriculture. That's about 10% of our footprint. Listen to this, across the world, that's 25%. So whatever we do here is going to be instructive. for what the rest of the world can learn from it to boot.",
